{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "language, having an abstract and describing factors contributing towards overweight and obesity. ... For this purpose, a computerbased search was performed on PubMed and PubGet to retrieve relevant articles. ... Women living in households with highest SES were more likely to be obese (23.3%) and overweight (34.8%) ... Finally, 6(22.2%) studies met the eligibility criteria and were entered in data extraction form (Table-1).",
      "reason": "Eligibility is partly specified via study population characteristics (women aged 15–49), time period (2005–2015), and requirement that studies describe factors contributing to overweight/obesity with an abstract; however, eligible study designs, settings, and follow-up requirements are not clearly specified."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "for a period of 10 years from 2005 to 2015.PubMed and PubGet were used as resource database. Search key terms were \"Socioeconomic status\", \"nutrition\", \"middle and low income countries\", language, having an abstract and describing factors contributing towards overweight and obesity. ... We included all papers published in the English",
      "reason": "Report characteristics such as publication window (2005–2015) and language (English) and that papers have an abstract are mentioned, but dissemination year, publication vs report status, and (where relevant) other report characteristic details are not fully specified."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No distinction is provided between exclusion because outcomes were not measured versus exclusion because outcome results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The evidence does not specify groups used in each synthesis and link them to comparisons defined in the review objectives."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Out of these, 20(74%) studies were excluded as 8(29%) did not report results stratified by SES; 2(7.5%) restricted to adolescents; 10(37%) did not include body mass index (BMI) as an outcome. One (3.7%) study was further excluded restricted to obesity in males.",
      "reason": "Rationales are provided for notable eligibility restrictions/exclusions (e.g., missing SES-stratified results, adolescent-only studies, missing BMI outcome, male-only obesity). However, the evidence does not clearly explain rationales for all notable restrictions, nor does it fully map restrictions back to specific eligibility criteria clauses."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 66
}

